                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A borderline thumbs up on this venerable poker-solitaire RPG battler.\n\nThe good:\nCool art and animations overall.\nDecent music and sound effects.\nThe core gameplay is fun.\nThe story is...sufficient.\n\nThe meh:\nThe AI is brutal. \nThere are a lot of systems under-explained, and simply grinding doesn't help build up your HP.\nHuge difficulty spikes. After 12 hours I can barely defeat enemies with comparable HP - how in blazes am I supposed to fight gatekeeper bosses with 10X as much?\nMonsters respawn on the map. Why exactly?\n\nThe verdict:\nI had a good time with this game for about 10 hours, so if you see it on sale, it might be worth it if you're into solitaire-based games like I am. But either I'm missing something (a likely scenario) or this game is just too hard.",
